<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-BHP 9-mth steel despatches up 4 pct.</title>
<headline>RTRS-BHP 9-mth steel despatches up 4 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia's biggest raw steel maker, The Broken Hill Pty Co Ltd, said on Tuesday that its steel despatches rose four percent to 6.189 million tonnes in the nine months to February, while its steelmake fell four percent to 6.231 million tonnes.  </p>
<p>BHP said in its latest production report that raw steel production for the month of February at 634,000 tonnes was below the same month last year due to unplanned maintenance at Port Kembla's No 5 blast furnace following a molten iron break-out and lower production from Sydney Steel Mill.</p>
<p>As well, BHP New Zealand Steel's February reporting period was four weeks in 1997 compared to five weeks in 1996.</p>
<p>Steelmaking at North Star BHP Steel in Delta, Ohio, was halted after an explosion on February 28. &quot;Repairs are underway with production expected to restart before the end of March.&quot;  </p>
<p>Steel despatches from Australian and New Zealand operations for February were eight percent above the same period last year.</p>
<p>Higher exports from Australia for February were mainly due to the timing of export shipments.</p>
